(ned UNLOAD SPINDLE -- physical drawbar release + PB software unload)
; ned I/O map (ned5_iron.hal): M64/M65 P0 = drawbar release ON/OFF
; (estop-gated via toolrel.permit); digital-in-00 = tool LOCKED sensor;
; digital-in-01 = tool RELEASED sensor; digital-in-02 = shaft stopped.
; The sim versions used the SIM's pin numbers (P2/P4/P5) -- on ned P4 is the
; chip blow-off. Every pin below is ned's.
o<unload_spindle> sub
; Spindle must be stopped -- and we STOP it, we do not merely complain.
; Operator 2026-08-11: "the spindle should be stopped the moment that button
; is pressed". The old code only read the sensor and aborted, which left the
; shaft turning. M5 commands the stop; M66 L3 then waits for the coast-down
; (no brake exists on this machine), and only a timeout aborts.
M5
M66 P2 L3 Q30
o<usp1> if [#5399 LT 0]
    (ABORT, unload_spindle: shaft never stopped -- not releasing)
o<usp1> endif
M64 P0
; wait for the tool-released sensor, up to 5 s
M66 P1 L3 Q5
o<usp2> if [#5399 LT 0]
    M65 P0
    (ABORT, unload_spindle: tool-released sensor never confirmed -- re-clamped)
o<usp2> endif
; DRAWBAR DWELL. The sensor confirms the cylinder REACHED its end state; it
; does not mean the air has settled or the taper has stopped moving. Wait
; before anything else happens (operator 2026-08-04: "i need that dwell for
; all drawbar actions. .5 second dwell"). Every drawbar action on the machine
; funnels through here -- M24 -> unclamptool, M25 -> clamptool -- so this one
; place covers m21/m22, toolchange, load/unload and the GUI buttons alike.
; #3975 (rack-atc-setup.user-2-param) tunes it; 0 or unset means 0.5 s, never
; no wait.
#<db_dwell> = #3975
o90 if [#<db_dwell> LE 0]
    #<db_dwell> = 0.5
o90 endif
G4 P#<db_dwell>

; PB software unload (spindle now empty)
M61 Q0
G49
#3991 = 0
(DEBUG, drawbar RELEASED -- remove the tool. Open until LOAD SPINDLE / M65 P0)

o<unload_spindle> endsub
M2 (end program)
